{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,14]],"date-time":"2025-06-14T12:44:45Z","timestamp":1749905085346,"version":"3.38.0"},"reference-count":38,"publisher":"SAGE Publications","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2017,7,1]],"date-time":"2017-07-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1498867200000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/3.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["journals.sagepub.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Revista Internacional de Educaci\u00f3n Musical"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2017,7]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> Musical notation appears as a problematic aspect in the debate about the forms of coloniality of knowledge. It is often seen as an instrument of domination because it imposes itself as a mode of representation for music coming from oral tradition, which finds innumerable limitations in the notation for its record. The epistemology of musical notation that is questioned here as hegemonic is that which: (i) limits its possibilities to academic repertoire; (ii) warns about its (in)ability to register other music; (iii) limits and reduces its function to that of a register; (iv) encourages the development of reading skills in particular; and (v) assumes the activity of reading as decoding and writing as codifying with its concomitant pedagogy. This epistemology entails a Eurocentric perspective of musical notation that has colonized music education, naturalizing not only in the fields of musical training, but also in ordinary life. <\/jats:p><jats:p> In this article we propose to question that epistemology, providing empirical evidence and arguments that allow us to estimate alternative assumptions for thinking about musical notation as a system of representation, with the consequent decolonial possibilities that this implies. <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.12967\/riem-2017-5-p129-138","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2018,1,18]],"date-time":"2018-01-18T15:27:06Z","timestamp":1516289226000},"page":"129-138","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1177\/sage-journals-update-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":6,"title":["Hacia una epistemolog\u00eda decolonial de la notaci\u00f3n musical"],"prefix":"10.1177","volume":"5","author":[{"given":"Mar\u00eda In\u00e9s","family":"Burcet","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Universidad Nacional de La Plata (Argentina)."}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"179","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2017,7,1]]},"reference":[{"key":"bibr1-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2307\/852110"},{"key":"bibr2-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138","first-page":"35","volume":"1","author":"Aguilar M. del C.","year":"1997","journal-title":"Orpheotron"},{"key":"bibr3-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1163\/9789087905286"},{"volume-title":"The mind behind the musical ear. How children develop musical intelligence.","year":"1991","author":"Bamberger J.","key":"bibr4-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"Estudios lingu\u00edsticos sobre la relaci\u00f3n entre oralidad y escritura.","year":"1998","author":"Blanche-Benveniste C.","key":"bibr5-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"Relaciones de (in)dependencia entre oralidad y escritura.","year":"2002","author":"Blanche-Benveniste C.","key":"bibr6-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"Actas de la Segunda Jornada de Desarrollo Auditivo en la Formaci\u00f3n del M\u00fasico Profesional.","year":"2010","author":"Burcet M. I.","key":"bibr7-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"Tradici\u00f3n y diversidad en los aspectos psicol\u00f3gicos, socioculturales y musicol\u00f3gicos de la formaci\u00f3n musical.","year":"2010","author":"Burcet M. I.","key":"bibr8-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"key":"bibr9-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138","unstructured":"BurcetM. I. (2014). Realidad perceptual de la nota como unidad operativa del pensamiento musical. Tesis de Maestr\u00eda, Facultad de Bellas Artes, UNLP, Argentina. Disponible en http:\/\/sedici.unlp.edu.ar\/handle\/10915\/41539."},{"volume-title":"Memorias de las II Jornadas Internacionales de Educaci\u00f3n Auditiva.","year":"2007","author":"Burcet M. I.","key":"bibr10-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"key":"bibr11-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138","unstructured":"BurcetM. I., y ShifresF. (2017). The conceptualizations that children of 8 years old do about the minimum units of musical segmentation. Trabajo presentado en el Global Arts and Psychology Seminar (GAPS). Gratz, del 28 al 29 de abril."},{"volume-title":"Actas del 120 ECCoM.","year":"2015","author":"Castro S. T.","key":"bibr12-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"key":"bibr13-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/oso\/9780198161547.001.0001"},{"volume-title":"Generative processes in music: The psychology of performance, improvisation, and composition.","year":"1988","author":"Davidson L.","key":"bibr14-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"Children and the art.","year":"1989","author":"Davidson L.","key":"bibr15-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"key":"bibr16-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2307\/3332965"},{"volume-title":"Experience and nature.","year":"1927","author":"Dewey J.","key":"bibr17-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"La m\u00fasica en Cartagena de Indias.","year":"1983","author":"Escobar L. A.","key":"bibr18-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"Alfabetizaci\u00f3n, teor\u00eda y pr\u00e1ctica.","year":"1997","author":"Ferreiro E.","key":"bibr19-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"Cultura escrita y educaci\u00f3n.","year":"1999","author":"Ferreiro E.","key":"bibr20-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"Relaciones de (in)dependencia entre oralidad y escritura.","year":"2002","author":"Ferreiro E.","key":"bibr21-RIEM-2017-5-p129-138"},{"volume-title":"Los sistemas de escritura en el desarrollo del ni\u00f1o.","y